    "created_at": "2025-05-26T20:49:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-26T20:49:41Z",
    "body": "I'm not aware of plans of it being implemented for `ping`.\r\n\r\nScripting is disabled check is used by lazy-loading, which is implemented ([see wpt](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/image-loading-lazy-in-script-disabled-iframe.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=lazy)). However, CSS can probably be used to \"ping\" when a link is clicked (with `:active`) or when something is scrolled into view (with scroll-driven animations).\r\n\r\nEither the CSS features need to also be have a scripting-disabled check, or the HTML features should keep working when scripting is disabled, I think.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
